      "id": "hook",
      "gapAfter": 0.3,
      "text": "Everyone thinks Nvidia wins on chips. That's wrong."
    },
    {
      "id": "rivals",
      "gapAfter": 0.3,
      "text": "AMD, Google and Amazon all build fast AI chips."
    },
    {
      "id": "money",
      "gapAfter": 0.35,
      "text": "Yet Nvidia still earns roughly 90% of its fiscal 2026 revenue from data centers."
    },
    {
      "id": "cuda",
      "gapAfter": 0.3,
      "text": "The reason is software. In 2006, Nvidia announced CUDA, its toolkit for programming GPUs."
    },
    {
      "id": "devs",
      "gapAfter": 0.3,
      "text": "Nvidia says 6 million developers build on it."
    },
    {
      "id": "switch",
      "gapAfter": 0.35,
      "text": "Switching chips often means rewriting years of code."
    },
    {
      "id": "payoff",
      "gapAfter": 0.45,
      "text": "For many teams, the moat isn't just the chip. It's the code."
    },
    {
      "id": "cta",
      "gapAfter": 0.5,
      "text": "Follow for part two: can anyone break CUDA's grip?"
    }
  ],
