  "analysis_points": [
    "The revenue mix shows demand is concentrated in data centers, not gaming or PCs.",
    "Switching cost is a large part of the moat: libraries (cuDNN, cuBLAS), custom kernels, tooling and team skills are CUDA-specific, so moving means porting work.",
    "Rivals can match chip speed; matching a 20-year software ecosystem is harder. Software is not the only advantage (networking, memory and supply also matter), but it is the hardest to copy."
  ],
